// class_inheritance_cycle_rejected.wi -- a class may not, directly or through
// its bases, extend itself.
//
// Every `extends` chain has to end at a class with no base. A chain that comes
// back to where it started is rejected with E0426, once per cycle, with every
// member labelled and the whole ring spelled out in a note:
//
//   open class A extends B { pub x: i64; }
//   open class B extends A { pub y: i64; }
//
//   error[E0426]: cyclic class inheritance involving `A`
//    --> ring.wi:1:6
//     |
//   1 | open class A extends B { pub x: i64; }
//     |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ class cannot transitively extend itself
//   2 | open class B extends A { pub y: i64; }
//     |      --------------------------------- `B` is part of the cycle
//     |
//   note: inheritance cycle: A extends B extends A
//   help: remove one `extends` so the chain ends at a class with no base
//
// The same applies to a class that names itself (`class A extends A`) and to a
// longer ring (`A extends B`, `B extends C`, `C extends A`). A class that only
// extends INTO a ring is not reported on its own: cutting the ring is the one
// fix, and the checks that need a finished base chain (constructor arity,
// base `init` rules, interface conformance) run again once it is cut. Before
// this rule existed the ring above either compiled silently (no fields) or
// crashed the compiler in codegen (with fields).
//
// The runnable program below is the shape the ring was probably reaching for:
// a chain that ends at a root, with each class adding its own field.

open class Root {
    pub x: i64;

    pub fn sum(self) -> i64 {
        return self.x;
    }
}

open class Mid extends Root {
    pub y: i64;
}

class Leaf extends Mid {
    pub z: i64;

    pub fn describe(self) -> String {
        return "Leaf: " + self.x.toString() + " " + self.y.toString() + " " + self.z.toString();
    }
}

fn main() {
    // The memberwise constructor takes the fields root-first: x, y, z.
    let leaf = new Leaf(1, 2, 3);
    println(leaf.describe());
    println("sum: " + (leaf.sum() + leaf.y + leaf.z).toString());
}
